message: "For work that uses SageCircuit, please reference this project."
title: "SageCircuit: a locally operated AI system"
version: "8.1.0"
date-released: "2026-10-20"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/gaurzamdev/SageCircuit"
keywords:
  - local-ai
  - from-scratch
  - transformer
  - mixture-of-experts
  - retrieval
  - sqlite
  - python
authors:
  - name: "Koustubh Gaikwad"
    alias: "Koustubh12345"
abstract: >-
  SageCircuit is a self-contained AI application for local use. It combines a
  compact Transformer/Mixture-of-Experts language component with retrieval
  from a SQLite knowledge store, deterministic solvers, a local browser chat,
  and an OpenAI-compatible API. It does not depend on Llama, GGUF, or
  pretrained weights.
